{"schema":2,"commit":"246cbcf015d044b518e487d4c43d27d832c1e5d9","branch":"main","base_sha":"dc12f30e47dfdb20990f51f7064ced2757c9c074","message":"feat: distribute through a Homebrew tap, keeping Electron out of the Cellar\n\nnpm publishing needs a token that is not available, so the primary channel is\nnow `brew install abdusselm/tap/panea`.\n\nHomebrew rewrites dylib IDs for every Mach-O file in its Cellar. With Electron\nvendored there, `brew install` printed:\n\n    Error: Failed changing dylib ID of .../Electron Framework.framework/.../libEGL.dylib\n    Error: Failed to fix install linkage\n\nwhich is precisely the signature damage this project exists to avoid, and it\nwould reach every user because the relocation is unconditional. So the formula\ninstalls only the JavaScript, and the Electron runtime goes to ~/.panea/electron\non the first `panea --app`. The keg went from 325.8 MB built in 76s, with two\nerrors, to 17.2 MB built in 11s, with none.\n\n- server/electron.js resolves the bundle from PANEA_ELECTRON_DIR, then the\n  package's node_modules, then ~/.panea/electron. Checkouts keep using\n  node_modules, so `npm run app` is unchanged.\n- scripts/ensure-electron.mjs downloads through @electron/get and unpacks with\n  ditto, into whichever directory targetDirFor picks.\n- bin/panea.js fetches and brands the runtime on demand when --app finds none.\n- server/update.js now reads GitHub releases rather than the npm registry, and\n  runs brew or npm depending on how panea was installed.\n- The release workflow creates the GitHub release and prints the formula\n  sha256; npm publishing is skipped unless an NPM_TOKEN secret exists.\n- scripts/update-tap.mjs writes Formula/panea.rb with that checksum.\n\nVerified end to end: brew install from a local tap is clean, the first --app\ndownloads and launches, the second starts instantly, no Mach-O lands in the\nCellar, and the checkout workflow still works.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018t9iga7qxv4tGRzZDQdBMM","coding_time_nanos":956278542000,"totals":{"added_lines":339,"ai_added_lines":339,"human_added_lines":0,"deleted_lines":70,"ai_deleted_lines":56,"human_deleted_lines":14,"files":10,"tokens":{"input":36,"output":20151,"cache_read":6711015,"cache_write":24080},"models":{"claude-opus-5":339}},"by_tool":{"claude":{"lines":339,"deleted_lines":56,"suggested_lines":737,"accepted_lines":339,"tokens":{"input":36,"output":20151,"cache_read":6711015,"cache_write":24080}}},"by_gen_type":{"chat":0,"cli":395,"completion":0,"human":14},"files":[{"path":".github/workflows/release.yml","type":"MODIFIED","added_lines":19,"deleted_lines":5,"ai_added_lines":19,"ai_deleted_lines":3,"human_deleted_lines":2,"lines":[{"start":14,"end":15,"type":"add","author_type":"AI","tool":"claude","model":"claude-opus-5","gen_type":"cli"},{"start":44,"end":44,"type":"delete","author_type":"AI","tool":"claude","model":"claude-opus-5","gen_type":"cli"},{"start":45,"end":46,"type":"delete","author_type":"Human"},{"start":47,"end":48,"type":"delete","author_type":"AI","tool":"claude","model":"claude-opus-5","gen_type":"cli"},{"start":50,"end":66,"type":"add","author_type":"AI","tool":"claude","model":"claude-opus-5","gen_type":"cli"}]},{"path":"CLAUDE.md","type":"MODIFIED","added_lines":12,"deleted_lines":0,"ai_added_lines":12,"lines":[{"start":74,"end":83,"type":"add","author_type":"AI","tool":"claude","model":"claude-opus-5","gen_type":"cli"},{"start":91,"end":92,"type":"add","author_type":"AI","tool":"claude","model":"claude-opus-5","gen_type":"cli"}]},{"path":"CONTRIBUTING.md","type":"MODIFIED","added_lines":15,"deleted_lines":3,"ai_added_lines":15,"ai_deleted_lines":3,"lines":[{"start":79,"end":79,"type":"add","author_type":"AI","tool":"claude","model":"claude-opus-5","gen_type":"cli"},{"start":79,"end":79,"type":"delete","author_type":"AI","tool":"claude","model":"claude-opus-5","gen_type":"cli"},{"start":80,"end":80,"type